ed as a capacitor. Any intended decoupling on the EthernetAndPower sheet is missing.\", \"confidence\": 0.45}, {\"category\": \"other\", \"components\": [\"U8\", \"J7\"], \"pins\": [\"U8.2\", \"U8.4\", \"J7.2\", \"U5.26\"], \"nets\": [\"Net-(U8-Pad2)\", \"Net-(U8-Pad4)\", \"UART_RX\"], \"observed\": \"The debug header J7.2 is driven by a 74LVC1G34 buffer U8 (input from UART_TXD0 on U5.26), not directly by the SKW92A UART TX pin.\", \"expected\": \"The spec states J7.2 connects directly to UART_TX (SKW92A pin 26), with no buffer in the path.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"J7 | Conn_01x03 | Debug UART header | netlist: pin1\u2192GND, pin2\u2192`UART_TX` (SKW92A pin 26)\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"J7\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pinfunction \\\"Pin_2\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\")) (node (ref \\\"U8\\\") (pin \\\"4\\\") (pintype \\\"output\\\"))\"}], \"impact\": \"The debug UART path differs from the spec. The buffer is powered from +3V3 and would be a functional change, though it likely does not stop the module booting.\", \"confidence\": 0.2}]}",
